  "$comment": "Accepted platform cfgs per production Rust file, seeded when the platform-seam convention landed: `negated` counts OS predicates under a `not(…)` (an arm for \"every other OS\"), `outsideSeam` counts OS cfgs outside a `platform/` directory. A strict ratchet: local runs lower each number to the current count and drop a file that reaches zero, and raising one needs David's OK (scripts/check/checks/DETAILS.md § Allowlist consent). The fix for a file over its number is to name the OSes an arm is for and move the split behind a seam (docs/guides/platform-seams.md), not to bump the number.",
